        "original_id": "79fc9612-c22f-55b2-8a1f-66e3bee326d1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Tawengwa\n- Places: Marondera, Southern Rhodesia, Zimbabwe\n- Properties: Zimdale farm\n- Topics: colonialism, racial segregation, land ownership\n\nFacts:\n- From 1923 to 1980, the Colony of Southern Rhodesia was a self-governing British Crown colony in southern Africa and the predecessor of modern Zimbabwe.\n- In 1960, George Tawengwa became the first Black person in Southern Rhodesia to purchase a commercial farm when he bought the 1,872.0-hectare Zimdale farm in Marondera from a white farmer.\n- George Tawengwa's 1960 purchase of Zimdale farm took place under the colonial system of Southern Rhodesia, which was ruled by a racist white minority.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
